# CONF-3 derivation input for the EXECUTION-LEASE floor
# (libs/repro_distributed_worker/c/repro_lease_linux.c, threat model G30).
#
# The floor's seccomp ALLOW-LIST is derived, not hand-picked:
#
#   allowed = expand(@system-service)        systemd's curated set for services,
#                                            expanded group by group by
#                                            `systemd-analyze syscall-filter`
#           + every `allow` line below       observed in the profiled lease
#                                            workload and not in that set
#           - every `deny` line below        removed from it, each with its reason
#
# and every other syscall is reported and refused (`syscall-denied`). Numbers
# come from the kernel UAPI headers of each architecture, not from the libc
# `SYS_*` macros of the build host, so no entry silently vanishes when a
# header is old. scripts/derive_lease_floor_syscalls.py turns this file into
# libs/repro_distributed_worker/c/repro_lease_floor_syscalls.h; `just lint`
# regenerates it on Linux and fails when the committed header differs.
#
# Argument-dependent rules live in the filter itself, beside the allow-list:
# socket() only for AF_INET/AF_INET6/AF_UNIX (creating a unix socket grants
# nothing; the supervisor refuses and reports a connect/sendto/sendmsg to any
# unix socket that EXISTS in the lease's view, and answers one that reaches
# nothing — the libc's nscd probe — with the kernel's own error, unreported:
# threat model G38); clone() never with a CLONE_NEW* flag;
# clone3() answered ENOSYS (its flags are in memory the filter cannot read;
# the C library falls back to clone()); personality() only the query and
# PER_LINUX.
#
# Profile: the lease workload of the five M7 worker tests and the lease
# confinement test (compilers, the shell, git-free test scripts, bash
# /dev/tcp egress probes), run under this floor with every denial reported;
# re-run whenever the workload changes (CONF-3).

# --- removed from @system-service -------------------------------------------
deny unshare             namespace construction: a lease's namespaces are the worker's to make (CONF-5), never the action's
deny setns               joining another namespace
deny kcmp                compares kernel objects across processes (process introspection)
deny process_madvise     acts on another process's memory
deny process_vm_readv    reads another process's memory
deny process_vm_writev   writes another process's memory
deny io_uring_setup      a second syscall interface the filter cannot see into
deny io_uring_enter      (io_uring)
deny io_uring_register   (io_uring)
deny userfaultfd         a kernel-exploitation primitive; no build or test needs it
deny keyctl              the kernel keyring (credentials that are not the lease's)
deny add_key             (keyring)
deny request_key         (keyring)

# --- observed in the lease workload, outside @system-service ----------------
# (none: the profiled workload stays inside @system-service minus the above)
